```js
const initialRotationY = mesh.rotation.y;
const rotationPeriodMs = 2000;
let startTime;

function animate(timestamp) {
  startTime ??= timestamp;

  const turns = (timestamp - startTime) / rotationPeriodMs;
  mesh.rotation.y = initialRotationY + turns * 2 * Math.PI;

  renderer.render(scene, camera);
  requestAnimationFrame(animate);
}

requestAnimationFrame(animate);
```

This proposes constant-speed Y rotation: 180° after one second and 360° after two seconds, independent of frame count. It never changes the material.

